		{
			dependencies: ["44EA00000000000A"]
			description: [
				"A &eDeployer&r is a tireless mechanical hand - it places, uses, and crafts on repeat. With a &eDepot&r as its workbench, it performs the assembly lines the next quest demands."
				""
				"&e&lIt does whatever you would do holding that item.&r Give it a sword and it attacks. A hoe, it tills. A bucket, it fills or empties. Bone meal, it fertilises. An empty hand, it punches. Whatever the item does when &lyou&r right-click, the Deployer does forever."
				""
				"&e&lTwo modes&r, toggled with the Wrench:"
				"&7- &fUse&7 - right-clicks, the default."
				"&7- &fPunch&7 - left-clicks. This is how you make it break blocks or fight."
				""
				"&e&lSequenced Assembly&r is what it is really here for. A Depot or belt carries a base item past a line of Deployers, each adding one component in order, and the last step spits out the finished part. That is how you make the &6Precision Mechanism&r - and the Precision Mechanism is the gate to all of Mekanism."
				""
				"&7Filter each Deployer so it only consumes the ingredient it is meant to. Unfiltered Deployers will happily grab the wrong item off the belt and ruin the sequence.&r"
				""
				"&8Feed them from a chest via funnels. A Deployer with an empty inventory silently does nothing, which looks identical to a broken build."
			]
			icon: "create:deployer"
			id: "44EA00000000000D"
			rewards: [{
				id: "44EA00000000010D"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			subtitle: "&7A tireless hand"
			tasks: [
