		{
			dependencies: ["44EA00000000000E"]
			description: [
				"&6Create Crafts & Additions&r bridges Forge Energy and kinetic energy. An &eAlternator&r turns rotation into FE for Mekanism/AE2; an &eAccumulator&r does the reverse, drawing FE to spin your cogs."
				""
				"&e&lThis is the single most important block in Age II.&r Everything after Create - Mekanism, AE2, Powah, RFTools - runs on Forge Energy. Water wheels make rotation. The Alternator is the only thing standing between the two, and it is what turns a Create build into a &lpower plant&r."
				""
				"&e&lHow to wire it:&r shaft into the Alternator, cable out. Output scales with the &lspeed&r of the rotation feeding it, so gear &lup&r before the Alternator, not down. A slow, high-torque line makes almost nothing."
				""
				"&e&lThe Accumulator runs it backwards&r - FE in, rotation out. Useful once you have a big electric grid and want to drive a Create machine from it without building a second water wheel."
				""
				"&7It also adds electric versions of Create blocks, an Electric Motor with adjustable RPM, and cables that carry FE without needing another mod's wiring.&r"
				""
				"&8Note: this pack now also has &fCreate: Power Grid&r, which simulates real electricity on top of Create. Crafts & Additions is the simple FE bridge; Power Grid is the deep end. You want this one first."
			]
			icon: "createaddition:alternator"
			id: "7592B47334DC838E"
			rewards: [{
				id: "35E70C6D60B1DCF6"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7FE meets kinetics"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "3568529EB4586055"
					item: "createaddition:alternator"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "6E2E4F44C1148700"
