			]
			title: "&eCreate Crafts & Additions"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["44EA00000000000E"]
			description: [
				"&6Create: Steam 'n' Rails&r adds trains. Lay &etrack&r, mount a &esemaphore&r for signaling, and top off a locomotive with a &econductor's cap&r before you drive it."
				""
				"&e&lOn a floating island, trains are not decoration.&r They are the cheapest way to move large amounts of material between platforms that are too far apart to belt and too close to justify an AE2 network."
				""
				"&e&lThe build order that works:&r"
				"&71.&r Lay &7Train Track&r with the &7Railway Casing&r - it auto-curves and bridges gaps, so you do not place every piece by hand."
				"&72.&r Place a &7Train Station&r beside the track and name it."
				"&73.&r Build the train on the track using a &7Train Assembler&r - bogeys first, then the body."
				"&74.&r Assemble from the station, then give it a &7Schedule&r."
				""
				"&e&lSchedules are the actual feature.&r A schedule is a little program - go to station A, wait until cargo full, go to station B, wait 30 seconds, repeat. Hand it to a &7Conductor&r and the train runs itself forever with no player nearby."
				""
				"&7Semaphores and signals stop two trains colliding on shared track. With one train you can skip them entirely.&r"
				""
				"&8Fully optional. Nothing in the progression requires a train - but hauling stacks of ore chunks across your island by hand gets old fast."
			]
			icon: "railways:semaphore"
			id: "6187A9055B14303B"
			rewards: [{
				id: "6A28B7F175FCB649"
